.TH NEW-AZURESTATICWEBAPP 1 "October 2026" "Noble Factor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
New-AzureStaticWebApp \- create a site's Azure resource group, Static Web App, Entra ID sign-in and GitHub Actions principal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B New-AzureStaticWebApp
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.B \-\-name
.I app-name
.B \-\-domain
.I custom-domain
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B New-AzureStaticWebApp
shows the subscription, tenant, location and names it will use, asks for confirmation, and then creates, in order:
.IP 1. 3
the resource group;
.IP 2. 3
the Static Web App, on the Standard SKU, which custom authentication requires;
.IP 3. 3
the Entra ID app registration
.IR app-name \-auth,
with the sign-in redirect URIs of the app's own hostname and of
.IR custom-domain ,
and a client secret good for two years;
.IP 4. 3
the deployment token, read from the app;
.IP 5. 3
the service principal
.RI sp\- app-name \-github,
Contributor on the resource group alone, for GitHub Actions; one that exists has its credentials reset.
.PP
Each that exists already is reported and kept.
It ends by printing, on standard output, the secrets each under its label, the DNS record to add, and the
.B az staticwebapp hostname set
command that registers the domain once DNS has propagated.
.BR New-SiteHosting (1)
reads the secrets back by their labels.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show this manual page and exit.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fIapp-name\fR
The application's name, from which the resources are named. Required.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-domain " " \fIcustom-domain\fR
The custom domain the site will answer at. Required.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION
The subscription. Default: the current one.
.TP
.B AZURE_LOCATION
The region. Default: westus2.
.TP
.B AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP
The resource group. Default: rg-\fIapp-name\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success \- the resources exist and the secrets are printed.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error \- a missing or invalid option.
.TP
.B 69
A tool it needs is not on PATH.
.TP
.B 75
Not confirmed; nothing was changed.
.TP
.B 77
Not logged in to Azure.
.TP
.B 72
Critical file missing \- \fBDeclare-BashScript\fR is not on PATH; deploy the base layer, NobleFactor/noblefactor-engprod.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bin/New-AzureStaticWebApp --name devlore-site --domain devlore.noblefactor.com
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR New-SiteHosting (1),
.BR Set-GitHubRepository (1),
.BR az (1)
